-- title:
--   Descent of strict ordinarity at odd p along a coefficient field map
-- statement:
--   Let $\psi\colon k\to k'$ be a ring homomorphism of fields and let $\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a $k$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_k V=2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho\colon \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to \mathrm{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite-dimensional intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ pointwise. Let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$. Assume that the adic representation attached to the scalar extension $k'\otimes_k V$ along $\psi$ is strictly ordinary at $p$, i.e. $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $k'$ (so $p=0$ in $k'$) and for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $P$ there is a $k'$-submodule $L'$ of $k'\otimes_k V$ spanned by the first vector of some basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, with $\sigma v-v\in L'$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$ inside the decomposition subgroup and all $v$, and such that each $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup admits $x,z$ with $\sigma$ acting on $L'$ by $x$, with $\sigma v-zv\in L'$ for all $v$, and with $x-az$ in the ideal generated by $p^n$ whenever $\sigma$ raises all $p^n$-th roots of unity to the power $a$. Then the adic representation attached to $\rho$ itself satisfies the same condition over $k$.
--
--   This is the descent, along an arbitrary homomorphism of coefficient fields and at an odd prime, of Wiles's strict ordinarity condition at $p$ for two-dimensional residual representations: the ordinary line may be chosen already over the smaller field. It is used in the passage from the Hecke-algebra side, where the residual representation is produced over a possibly larger residue field, to the representation over the field of interest, being cited by [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.isStrictOrdinaryAt_of_ringHom_of_dvd_of_not_isFlatAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.isStrictOrdinaryAt_of_ringHom_of_dvd_of_not_isFlatAt).
